<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Mathematical Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Lower Bound for 𝑇-step Parallel Decoding). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step parallel decoding model is defined by the factorization:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(Y|X)=\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(Y|X)=\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can decompose the true data distribution according to the partition <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)=\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)=\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these decompositions into the KL divergence formula, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)\;\|\;P_{\theta}(Y|X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)\;\|\;P_{\theta}(Y|X))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)}{P_{\theta}(Y|X)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)}{P_{\theta}(Y|X)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}{P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{P_{\text{data}}}\left[\log\frac{P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}{P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">At each step <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the model assumes conditional independence among the tokens in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> given the context <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,S_{&lt;i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,S_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})=\prod_{y_{j}\in S_{i}}P_{\theta}(y_{j}|X,S_{&lt;i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})=\prod_{y_{j}\in S_{i}}P_{\theta}(y_{j}|X,S_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by applying <a href="#S3.E1" title="In Parallel Decoding ‣ 3 Preliminaries: Diffusion LLM Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> from <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminaries: Diffusion LLM Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\geq\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\geq\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">By substituting this lower bound back into our sum, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min\nolimits_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\nolimits_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)\;\|\;P_{\theta}(Y|X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(Y|X)\;\|\;P_{\theta}(Y|X))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\nolimits_{\theta}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\nolimits_{\theta}\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\min\nolimits_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\min\nolimits_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{data}}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})\;\|\;P_{\theta}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Monotonicity of Error Bounds). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Subadditivity of Conditional Total Correlation)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let a set of random variables <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be partitioned into two disjoint subsets <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=A\cup B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=A\cup B</annotation></semantics></math>). For any conditioning context <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional total correlation of <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is lower-bounded as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(S|Z)\geq\mathcal{C}(A|Z)+\mathbb{E}_{A\sim P_{\text{data}}(A|Z)}[\mathcal{C}(B|Z,A)]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(S|Z)\geq\mathcal{C}(A|Z)+\mathbb{E}_{A\sim P_{\text{data}}(A|Z)}[\mathcal{C}(B|Z,A)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Subadditivity of Conditional Total Correlation). ‣ A.2 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Proofs ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of conditional total correlation (<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(S|Z)=\sum_{y\in S}H(y|Z)-H(S|Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(S|Z)=\sum_{y\in S}H(y|Z)-H(S|Z)</annotation></semantics></math>), we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}(A|Z)+\mathbb{E}_{A}[\mathcal{C}(B|Z,A)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}(A|Z)+\mathbb{E}_{A}[\mathcal{C}(B|Z,A)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)-H(A|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z,A)-H(B|Z,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)-H(A|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z,A)-H(B|Z,A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)-H(A|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z)-H(B|Z,A)\quad(\text{since }H(y_{b}|Z)\geq H(y_{b}|Z,A))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>since </mtext><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)-H(A|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z)-H(B|Z,A)\quad(\text{since }H(y_{b}|Z)\geq H(y_{b}|Z,A))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z)\right)-(H(A|Z)+H(B|Z,A))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{y_{a}\in A}H(y_{a}|Z)+\sum_{y_{b}\in B}H(y_{b}|Z)\right)-(H(A|Z)+H(B|Z,A))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in S}H(y|Z)-H(A,B|Z)\quad\text{(by the chain rule of entropy)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>(by the chain rule of entropy)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in S}H(y|Z)-H(A,B|Z)\quad\text{(by the chain rule of entropy)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{C}(S|Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{C}(S|Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Monotonicity of Error Bounds). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{i}^{*}\}_{i=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{i}^{*}\}_{i=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step partition that achieves the minimum error bound <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. We construct a <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-step partition <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by splitting the last set of the optimal partition, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, into two non-empty, disjoint subsets <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}^{*}=A\cup B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}^{*}=A\cup B</annotation></semantics></math>). The new partition is <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{1}^{*},\dots,S_{T-1}^{*},A,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{1}^{*},\dots,S_{T-1}^{*},A,B\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}^{*}\}_{i=1}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}^{*}\}_{i=1}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;i}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{T}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;i}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{T}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;i}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(A|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(B|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*},A)]\quad\text{(by \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{lemma:subadditivity})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>(by </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Subadditivity of Conditional Total Correlation). ‣ A.2 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Proofs ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}^{*}|X,S_{&lt;i}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(A|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*})]+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{C}(B|X,S_{&lt;T}^{*},A)]\quad\text{(by \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{lemma:subadditivity})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1})\quad\text{(by \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{theorem1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>(by </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Lower Bound for 𝑇-step Parallel Decoding). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1})\quad\text{(by \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{theorem1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\min\nolimits_{\{S_{k}\}_{k=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S_{k}\}_{k=1}^{T+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\min\nolimits_{\{S_{k}\}_{k=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S_{k}\}_{k=1}^{T+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Extended Version of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Monotonicity of Error Bounds). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotonicity of Error Bounds for Input-Dependent Partitions)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any given input <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)</annotation></semantics></math> be the error bound for a specific T-step partition <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X):=\textstyle\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}(\cdot|X)}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">data</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X):=\textstyle\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{S_{&lt;i}\sim P_{\text{data}}(\cdot|X)}[\mathcal{C}(S_{i}|X,S_{&lt;i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal T-step error bound, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the expected value of the minimum error bound over all possible partitions for each input:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}:=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">data</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}:=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim P_{\text{data}}}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically decreasing with respect to the number of generation steps:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Monotonicity of Error Bounds for Input-Dependent Partitions). ‣ A.3 Extended Version of ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Proofs ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by establishing a pointwise inequality for any single, arbitrary input <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us consider a special data distribution concentrated entirely on this single input <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the conclusion of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Monotonicity of Error Bounds). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of Parallel Decoding ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> to this special case directly establishes the following relationship. The optimal T-step error for this distribution (which is simply the optimal error for the input <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>) is greater than or equal to the optimal (T+1)-step error:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|x)\geq\min\nolimits_{\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}|x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|x)\geq\min\nolimits_{\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the expectation of this pointwise inequality <a href="#A1.E30" title="In Proof of . ‣ A.3 Extended Version of ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Proofs ‣ ParallelBench: Understanding the Trade-offs of Parallel Decoding in Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> over the true data distribution <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> directly yields the final result:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}:=\mathbb{E}_{X}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)\right]\geq\mathbb{E}_{X}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}|X)\right]=:\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}:=\mathbb{E}_{X}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}}\mathcal{L}_{T}(\{S_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}|X)\right]\geq\mathbb{E}_{X}\left[\min\nolimits_{\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}}\mathcal{L}_{T+1}(\{S^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{T+1}|X)\right]=:\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T}\geq\mathcal{L}^{*}_{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Further Discussion on Related Work</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Additional Unmasking Methods</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent work on Masked Diffusion Models (MDMs) has focused on optimizing the unmasking process to improve inference efficiency and generation quality. Besides the unmasking methods studied in this work, several additional methods target acceleration through parallel decoding. For instance, the EB-Sampler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ben-Hamu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> adaptively unmasks the largest group of tokens whose cumulative entropy falls below a threshold, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, achieving a 2–3<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> speedup. Similarly, the Dilated Unmasking Scheduler (DUS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luxembourg et al., 2025</a>)</cite> uses a deterministic, coarse-to-fine schedule to unmask non-adjacent tokens, reducing the number of denoiser calls within a block of size <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log B)</annotation></semantics></math>. The SlowFast Sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2025</a>)</cite> alternates between slow, exploratory phases and fast, parallel decoding phases, yielding up to a 15.6<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> speedup.
Other works focus on generation quality.
The PC-Sampler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, for example, corrects for biases in uncertainty-based sampling by using a composite score that combines a position-aware weight with a frequency-calibrated confidence score, improving performance by over 10%.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Related Benchmarks</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To contextualize our work, we review several key benchmarks commonly used to evaluate the capabilities of LLMs across different domains.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GSM8K</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Grade School Math 8K (GSM8K) dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite> is a prominent benchmark designed to assess the multi-step mathematical reasoning abilities of LLMs. It consists of thousands of grade-school-level word problems that require a sequence of logical steps and arithmetic operations to solve. The primary evaluation metric is final answer accuracy, where the model’s generated solution must exactly match the correct numerical result. Success on GSM8K is considered a strong indicator of a model’s capacity for complex, chain-of-thought reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">HumanEval</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The HumanEval benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021a</a>)</cite> is a standard for evaluating the code generation capabilities of models. The task involves completing Python function bodies based on a given function signature and a descriptive docstring. The dataset contains 164 such programming challenges of varying difficulty. Performance is measured by functional correctness, typically using the pass@<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021b</a>)</cite> metric.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SAMSum</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The SAMSum dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gliwa et al., 2019</a>)</cite> is tailored for the task of abstractive summarization of natural, real-world dialogues. It contains short, informal conversations, requiring a model to produce a concise summary that captures the main points of the exchange. The standard evaluation protocol relies on the ROUGE score <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin, 2004</a>)</cite>, which measures the n-gram overlap between the model-generated summary and one or more human-written reference summaries. While ROUGE is effective for assessing content overlap, our work diverges by focusing on the grammatical correctness and fluency of the generated summaries, aspects of quality not fully captured by lexical metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ChatGPT-Paraphrases</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ChatGPT-Paraphrases dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vladimir Vorobev, 2023</a>)</cite> is designed for evaluating a model’s ability to rephrase sentences while preserving their original semantic meaning. The dataset provides pairs of original sentences and their corresponding paraphrases. This benchmark is crucial for assessing a model’s fine-grained understanding of language and its capacity for fluent and diverse text generation, which are core skills for sophisticated natural language processing applications. While standard evaluations for this task often rely on semantic similarity metrics, our approach is different. Similar to SAMSum, we are primarily interested in the grammatical evaluation of the output.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Discrete Diffusion Strategies</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In discrete diffusion, a common strategy is the absorbing state approach, also known as masked diffusion. This method corrupts data by progressively replacing original tokens with a single, special <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> token. The key advantage of this technique lies in its reverse process. The model’s task is simplified to “filling in the blanks” at known <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> locations, which provides a very direct and clear learning signal. This is the primary approach used by many prominent open-source models, such as LLaDA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and Dream <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the uniform transition approach corrupts data differently. Instead of using a special token, it substitutes an existing token with any other token from the vocabulary, with each possibility having an equal probability of occurrence. This method gradually transforms the input into a sequence of purely random tokens. Consequently, the reverse process is more complex: the model must predict the original token from a noisy, corrupted one, rather than from a designated blank slate. Some recent models, including SEDD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, have explored this uniform approach.</p>
</div>
</section>
